WEBVTT

00:19.853 --> 00:24.258
The wound inside my sealed memories

00:24.258 --> 00:28.896
When it silently touches the heart

00:28.896 --> 00:36.029
Tears of loneliness behind
the gentle smile

00:36.570 --> 00:41.375
I seek boundless strength

00:41.375 --> 00:52.115
I continue to run up with
what I believe in

00:52.219 --> 00:54.321
I want to protect

00:54.321 --> 00:56.557
I want to believe

00:56.557 --> 01:00.828
all the reasons for that smile

01:00.828 --> 01:05.265
The heat and the love

01:05.265 --> 01:09.503
I accept them all

01:09.503 --> 01:13.107
I won't let go of your hand again

01:13.107 --> 01:21.242
Aiming towards that light...

01:36.597 --> 01:38.656
Mokkun! This way!

01:50.077 --> 01:51.712
Hey, you!

01:51.712 --> 01:53.814
The giant skull that's
attacking this village!

01:53.814 --> 01:55.949
You don't know who
you're dealing with, do you?!

01:55.949 --> 01:58.585
Yeah, you tell him, Mokkun!

01:58.585 --> 02:01.255
This Masahiro may seem
like a child...

02:01.255 --> 02:04.291
Inexperienced, and not
very powerful right now...

02:04.291 --> 02:06.560
But with a lot of training
and effort,

02:06.560 --> 02:09.163
he'll probably become
a great onmyouji...

02:09.163 --> 02:11.398
and defeat you easily in future!

02:11.398 --> 02:14.201
- So, back off!
- Wait a minute, Mokkun!

02:14.201 --> 02:16.837
I thought you were
supposed to back me up!

02:16.837 --> 02:19.169
I'm just being honest
with the guy.

02:26.080 --> 02:27.843
Let's get out of here!

02:44.998 --> 02:48.627
- Pull yourself together!
- I know that!

02:53.240 --> 02:56.107
[chant]

02:56.743 --> 03:02.841
[chant]

03:04.818 --> 03:06.587
I call upon the descending gods...

03:06.587 --> 03:09.523
and ask them to give me the
power to bind this demon,

03:09.523 --> 03:12.492
banish its evil and eliminate
the hundred devils now!

03:24.371 --> 03:26.206
It's finally over...

03:26.206 --> 03:28.509
You've really improved,
haven't you?

03:28.509 --> 03:30.911
As expected from
Abe no Seimei's grandson.

03:30.911 --> 03:34.248
Well then, I can go back
and get some rest.

03:34.248 --> 03:37.284
- Yeah, I'm worn out too.
- Why are you tired?

03:37.284 --> 03:39.286
You hardly did anything
at all, Mokkun!

03:39.286 --> 03:41.488
How dare you say that?

03:41.488 --> 03:43.457
I tagged along to make sure...

03:43.457 --> 03:45.893
that you wouldn't get
into trouble.

03:45.893 --> 03:49.630
Oh, I still remember that
cute little Masahiro.

03:49.630 --> 03:53.133
- He's all grown up now.
- Cute and little?!

03:53.133 --> 03:55.035
I'm already thirteen years old.

03:55.035 --> 03:57.936
And you and I met
only a month ago!

03:58.906 --> 04:00.874
What was that?

04:06.813 --> 04:10.010
This Youth, Seimei's Successor

04:12.853 --> 04:15.622
Oh, look. That's the
young grandson...

04:15.622 --> 04:18.559
of the great onmyouji,
Abe no Seimei.

04:18.559 --> 04:22.462
I see! I wonder why he's
interested in calligraphy.

04:22.462 --> 04:25.699
It seems that though he was
born of the Abe bloodline,

04:25.699 --> 04:27.634
he doesn't have the
second sight.

04:27.634 --> 04:32.206
So you're saying that he can't
sense spirits and demons?

04:32.206 --> 04:33.574
That's right.

04:33.574 --> 04:37.704
So now he's planning to become
a calligrapher instead...

04:43.717 --> 04:47.312
I guess I'm not meant
to be a calligrapher either.

04:51.558 --> 04:54.186
That hurt...

04:54.995 --> 04:57.190
It talked...

04:57.698 --> 05:00.267
- What are you staring at?
- Wait!

05:00.267 --> 05:03.237
Why am I able to see
this mononoke?

05:03.237 --> 05:06.573
Has my second sight finally
returned after all this time?!

05:06.573 --> 05:10.441
The sight I used to have
when I was a kid!

05:11.278 --> 05:14.615
So can you see that
mononoke? Or that one...

05:14.615 --> 05:17.311
Or the other one that's
standing right over there?

05:18.585 --> 05:21.088
- There are more?
- They are everywhere.

05:21.088 --> 05:23.352
I was afraid of that...

05:24.424 --> 05:26.793
Then why is it that
I can see you?

05:26.793 --> 05:29.596
Well that's because
I'm a very old spirit...

05:29.596 --> 05:31.798
and a very
powerful one too.

05:31.798 --> 05:36.003
That's why even someone
like you can see me.

05:36.003 --> 05:37.671
Geez...

05:37.671 --> 05:40.707
Aren't you that
Seimei's grandson?

05:40.707 --> 05:44.077
You were the one walking with
him some time ago, right?

05:44.077 --> 05:47.814
So what are you doing here,
Seimei's grandson?

05:47.814 --> 05:51.285
Stop calling me his
grandson! I'm Masahiro.

05:51.285 --> 05:55.915
Abe no Masahiro! So what if
my grandfather is famous!

05:57.824 --> 06:00.560
If there's something that's
bothering you, I'll listen.

06:00.560 --> 06:04.031
- Seimei's grandson, Masahiro...
- Whatever...

06:04.031 --> 06:08.058
This is... a calligraphy kit,
isn't it?

06:08.769 --> 06:12.406
Your expression says that you
gave up trying to be an onmyouji,

06:12.406 --> 06:15.842
and took up calligraphy.
But you failed at that too.

06:16.910 --> 06:19.980
Don't worry about your
bad handwriting!

06:19.980 --> 06:23.517
Or were you told that
you have no talent at all?

06:23.517 --> 06:24.851
Guess I'm right...

06:24.851 --> 06:29.220
Thank you for your interest
and concern, Mr. Mononoke.

06:42.869 --> 06:45.305
Geez, you're hurting my ears.

06:45.305 --> 06:48.208
Hey, what on earth!
How did you get in?!

06:48.208 --> 06:50.277
Hm? Through the gate...

06:50.277 --> 06:51.878
That's not what I meant!

06:51.878 --> 06:55.315
The house is protected by my
grandfather's magical barrier!

06:55.315 --> 06:59.019
Mononoke and spirits
should not be able to get in.

06:59.019 --> 07:01.510
But I got in, didn't I?

07:06.626 --> 07:07.861
What are you doing?

07:07.861 --> 07:10.931
Before my grandfather
or my father finds you...

07:10.931 --> 07:15.231
- Get out of here right now.
- Hey, it's raining out here!

07:28.081 --> 07:32.352
I can't believe you keep coming
to see me day after day...

07:32.352 --> 07:34.688
Oh, you noticed?

07:34.688 --> 07:38.825
You keep trying day after
day without giving up...

07:38.825 --> 07:40.827
It's the flute today?

07:40.827 --> 07:43.318
Don't ask me how it went.

07:46.633 --> 07:48.191
What's going on?!

07:52.205 --> 07:54.141
What... What was that?!

07:54.141 --> 07:56.777
- Princess!
- Hurry... Hurry up!

07:56.777 --> 07:58.870
Is it some kind of monster?!

08:02.382 --> 08:05.252
This... This is a demon
or something, right?

08:05.252 --> 08:08.088
- I've got to do something!
- Wait a minute!

08:08.088 --> 08:11.057
I'll give you credit for
your enthusiasm,

08:11.057 --> 08:14.661
but that's only because
you can't see it!

08:14.661 --> 08:18.064
- What kind of spirit do you see?
- It's a really scary one.

08:18.064 --> 08:20.634
It ate that big ox
in one bite!

08:20.634 --> 08:23.899
One bite?!! But... I must go!

08:26.673 --> 08:28.775
- What the?!
- It's fine if you were Seimei.

08:28.775 --> 08:31.801
But you can't possibly battle
a creature this powerful!

08:34.614 --> 08:38.318
- What happened to my carriage?
- Princess, keep your composure.

08:38.318 --> 08:39.717
Where's my carriage?

08:41.021 --> 08:43.723
I'm home, Father.

08:43.723 --> 08:46.487
Oh, welcome back. Come in.

08:49.529 --> 08:51.431
So, how did it go?

08:51.431 --> 08:54.332
What did the flute master
have to say?

08:54.768 --> 08:58.864
He said I could come over
and play for fun anytime.

08:59.506 --> 09:02.100
Play for fun... I see...

09:02.409 --> 09:04.978
Did he say any other
interesting things?

09:04.978 --> 09:09.182
What? Oh, not really...

09:09.182 --> 09:12.219
- Is that so?
- Yes, nothing!

09:12.219 --> 09:14.210
Well, all right then...

09:14.888 --> 09:17.657
There's a letter for you.

09:17.657 --> 09:19.459
It's from your grandfather.

09:19.459 --> 09:22.095
A letter? From grandfather?

09:22.095 --> 09:24.256
But we live in the same house...

09:26.566 --> 09:30.263
- I should read it, right?
- Of course.

09:37.410 --> 09:40.971
Yoshimasa has told me
the whole story.

09:43.483 --> 09:45.819
Masahiro, I've been told that...

09:45.819 --> 09:48.855
you no longer want to
become an onmyouji?

09:48.855 --> 09:52.125
This makes me very, very sad.

09:52.125 --> 09:54.928
I remember how you would
follow me around,

09:54.928 --> 09:59.666
calling out, "Grandpa, Grandpa"
when you were still a little boy.

09:59.666 --> 10:01.334
How is that related?

10:01.334 --> 10:04.271
Do you remember that
you could see...

10:04.271 --> 10:07.240
many different things
at that time?

10:07.674 --> 10:13.413
That's why I taught you the
secrets of my mystical powers.

10:13.413 --> 10:17.651
Thus, I'm going to entrust
you with an important task.

10:17.651 --> 10:19.243
What?!

10:19.920 --> 10:24.324
Some spirit has been making
trouble in the town recently.

10:24.324 --> 10:26.493
The villagers are frightened.

10:26.493 --> 10:29.229
The disturbances have
become so serious...

10:29.229 --> 10:32.032
that it breaks my heart
when I think of their fear...

10:32.032 --> 10:35.302
So, Masahiro, I want you
to exorcise it for me.

10:35.302 --> 10:37.804
I want you to exorcise
it for me.

10:37.804 --> 10:41.207
He makes it sound like
a simple errand.

10:41.207 --> 10:43.276
I see. You're here again?

10:43.276 --> 10:45.946
Well, don't blame me
if my father...

10:45.946 --> 10:49.816
finds a mononoke like you
here and casts you out.

10:49.816 --> 10:54.788
Cut it out, will you? And stop
calling me a mononoke!

10:54.788 --> 10:59.025
Anyway, a mononoke is a dead
soul that haunts people.

10:59.025 --> 11:03.463
You're Seimei's grandson and
you don't know the difference?!

11:03.463 --> 11:05.165
You're an ayakashi then!

11:05.165 --> 11:08.268
You're not wrong,
but that's kind of bland...

11:08.268 --> 11:10.170
All right, something
paranormal then.

11:10.170 --> 11:12.730
Hey, be serious about it!

11:16.009 --> 11:17.777
If you complain that much,

11:17.777 --> 11:21.481
just tell me your name
and I'll call you that?

11:21.481 --> 11:24.075
Well, I... can't do that...

11:24.851 --> 11:27.420
- Suit yourself!
- A name is something...

11:27.420 --> 11:31.157
that has a special meaning. You
can't give it out carelessly.

11:31.157 --> 11:34.127
You don't even know that?
You're Seimei's grandson!

11:34.127 --> 11:37.797
Fine! Then I call you
Mokkun the Mononoke!

11:37.797 --> 11:39.697
I've decided.

11:40.233 --> 11:41.801
What's that?!

11:41.801 --> 11:45.071
I have a much more refined
and elegant name than that!

11:45.071 --> 11:47.273
Calling me Mokkun
is so insulting!

11:47.273 --> 11:49.843
Mokkun, Mokkun,
Mokkun the Mononoke.

11:49.843 --> 11:51.834
- And that's final!
- Hey!

11:57.917 --> 11:59.819
Well, if you took out...

11:59.819 --> 12:02.389
your divination board and
reading books,

12:02.389 --> 12:05.625
I guess you're going to obey
Seimei and exorcise the demon?

12:05.625 --> 12:08.828
If I tell him that
I can't do it, he'll say...

12:08.828 --> 12:11.765
"I see. That's because you
haven't had enough training".

12:11.765 --> 12:14.000
And "Now I'll have to
teach you...

12:14.000 --> 12:17.037
all over again from
the beginning."

12:17.037 --> 12:19.139
He'd definitely say that!

12:19.139 --> 12:21.941
I'm not going to let him
get the better of me!

12:21.941 --> 12:24.044
I'll exorcise that demon
no matter what!

12:24.044 --> 12:25.545
Even if you can't see it?

12:25.545 --> 12:27.547
That's right.
So what if I can't see it?

12:27.547 --> 12:31.017
If you don't have the second
sight, the exorcism won't be easy.

12:31.017 --> 12:33.887
And you won't even know
if you're in danger.

12:33.887 --> 12:36.822
I don't care about that.
I have to try!

12:45.365 --> 12:47.765
Do you want to become
my eyes?

12:58.578 --> 13:01.581
I've never heard of an
onmyouji using a spirit...

13:01.581 --> 13:04.150
as a replacement for
the second sight.

13:04.150 --> 13:05.685
Whatever works.

13:05.685 --> 13:09.556
Hey, do you think this demon
that's been making trouble...

13:09.556 --> 13:11.658
is the same one
we ran into last time?

13:11.658 --> 13:15.095
Most likely it's the one
that ate the ox and carriage.

13:15.095 --> 13:17.797
The one that swallowed
a whole ox in one bite.

13:17.797 --> 13:19.788
Is it somewhere around here?

13:20.533 --> 13:23.195
No, I don't sense anything yet.

13:23.536 --> 13:26.539
Seimei taught you
the art of onmyou magic...

13:26.539 --> 13:28.908
when you were little,
didn't he?

13:28.908 --> 13:32.412
Yeah, they are all
in my head.

13:32.412 --> 13:34.581
But I've never used them before.

13:34.581 --> 13:36.182
Figured as much.

13:36.182 --> 13:39.853
And he gives you something
this big as your first task.

13:39.853 --> 13:43.857
Exactly! Usually, you'd start
out with something easy.

13:43.857 --> 13:46.493
Like helping someone who
complains of a heavy shoulder,

13:46.493 --> 13:49.629
or exorcising someone
that's been possessed.

13:49.629 --> 13:52.860
That's the sort of job you give
someone on their first task.

13:55.769 --> 13:57.566
Can you sense it?

13:58.271 --> 14:00.967
Yeah, it's the same one.

14:01.441 --> 14:03.375
It's this way.

14:03.476 --> 14:06.240
Right, that's what
I was thinking.

14:13.753 --> 14:15.653
Here it comes.

14:16.890 --> 14:19.256
Geez! We should run!

14:19.726 --> 14:21.694
The demon is burrowing
through the ground!

14:21.694 --> 14:23.525
This way!

14:28.768 --> 14:30.565
Is it gone?

14:32.539 --> 14:35.303
- No!
- It's still coming!

14:37.243 --> 14:40.076
- Stop right here!
- What? Oh, right!

14:41.147 --> 14:42.876
All right, retreat!

14:46.519 --> 14:48.555
- What's wrong?
- S-Something...

14:48.555 --> 14:50.682
Something's... got my foot!

14:51.991 --> 14:53.526
It's the demon's tongue.

14:53.526 --> 14:56.095
The demon has wrapped its
tongue around your foot!

14:56.095 --> 14:57.931
- No way!
- Don't let it drag you in.

14:57.931 --> 15:00.166
- Brace yourself!
- W-What's happening?

15:00.166 --> 15:02.235
Where is it trying
to drag me to?

15:02.235 --> 15:05.505
The demon is dragging you
towards its huge, open mouth!

15:05.505 --> 15:08.241
I'm not going to let it
eat me! I'll try a spell!

15:08.241 --> 15:11.506
[chant]

15:12.846 --> 15:14.609
Masahiro!

15:16.583 --> 15:18.107
Mokkun!

15:23.223 --> 15:25.225
Mokkun, what are you doing?!

15:25.225 --> 15:28.595
Go now! Get away
while you can!

15:28.595 --> 15:31.264
You're holding the demon's
jaws open, aren't you?

15:31.264 --> 15:33.800
- You can see it?!
- I don't need to see it...

15:33.800 --> 15:37.036
to know what you're doing!
This is its mouth!

15:37.036 --> 15:40.506
If I let go, it'll devour you!

15:40.506 --> 15:42.342
You're not strong
enough to fight it!

15:42.342 --> 15:44.944
I'm stronger than you!

15:44.944 --> 15:48.505
If you die here, I'll be
the one in deep trouble!

15:48.715 --> 15:51.251
Why would a stray mononoke
sacrifice so much for me?

15:51.251 --> 15:54.153
Don't worry about it.
Just get out of here!

15:54.153 --> 15:56.089
I can't just leave you here!

15:56.089 --> 15:58.558
I... will do something!

15:58.558 --> 16:00.727
If I can't even save
one little mononoke,

16:00.727 --> 16:03.463
how can I surpass
my grandfather?!

16:03.463 --> 16:06.728
You'll be eaten if
I don't do something!

16:09.402 --> 16:12.038
You're beginning to see it,
aren't you?

16:12.038 --> 16:14.641
That's not what's
important now!

16:14.641 --> 16:17.377
It's meaningless if we
don't survive this together!

16:17.377 --> 16:19.746
If you can see it, then
you should know that...

16:19.746 --> 16:22.181
you can't win this.
Hurry, go!!

16:22.181 --> 16:26.584
I wouldn't be happy to survive
if I have to sacrifice you!

16:27.520 --> 16:30.657
I'm aiming to become
a great onmyouji.

16:30.657 --> 16:32.258
One who won't sacrifice
anyone.

16:32.258 --> 16:34.886
That's what I needed... to hear!

16:35.561 --> 16:38.364
- Mokkun?
- My name's not Mokkun.

16:38.364 --> 16:43.269
Listen Masahiro,
I'll tell you my real name.

16:43.269 --> 16:45.305
This name has been
spoken by...

16:45.305 --> 16:48.141
only one person since
it was given to me.

16:48.141 --> 16:50.476
You may call me by that name.

16:50.476 --> 16:53.146
Could we pick a better time
to talk about names?

16:53.146 --> 16:55.842
Masahiro! Just say it!

17:03.189 --> 17:07.853
Listen! My name is Guren!
The Crimson Lotus!!

17:09.629 --> 17:11.392
Guren?

17:11.597 --> 17:13.766
That's right. Call my name!

17:13.766 --> 17:16.135
- Mo... Mokkun!
- No!

17:16.135 --> 17:18.433
Guren!

17:37.924 --> 17:40.119
What... is this?

17:42.095 --> 17:45.428
Where's the demon?
I have to save Mokkun!

17:55.008 --> 17:58.136
Hey, you have to do better than
that, Seimei's grandson!

17:59.045 --> 18:02.448
- It can't be! Mokkun?!
- It's Guren.

18:02.448 --> 18:04.717
And you have
a terrible memory.

18:04.717 --> 18:08.221
It is you, Mokkun!
I'm so glad you're alive!

18:08.221 --> 18:12.058
We meet again, Touda!

18:12.058 --> 18:13.855
Touda?

18:14.727 --> 18:19.323
Masahiro, isn't there something
that you should do right now?

18:20.366 --> 18:24.700
- I have to exorcise this worm!
- Foolish boy!

18:29.842 --> 18:33.334
[chant]

18:38.351 --> 18:41.521
Army of light that fights
the forces of darkness.

18:41.521 --> 18:43.148
Go forth and destroy!

18:58.805 --> 19:01.069
Geez, I'm exhausted...

19:02.375 --> 19:04.210
Touda...

19:04.210 --> 19:08.510
That demon called you
Touda, didn't it?

19:09.015 --> 19:11.384
- Did he really?
- Oh!

19:11.384 --> 19:13.653
Touda is one of the
Land Spirits...

19:13.653 --> 19:13.820
Touda
Touda is one of the
Land Spirits...

19:13.820 --> 19:15.855
Touda
on the Globe of the
Five Justices!

19:15.855 --> 19:16.122
on the Globe of the
Five Justices!

19:16.122 --> 19:18.750
You're Grandfather's
shikigami!

19:20.493 --> 19:23.262
But why are you using
the name Guren?

19:23.262 --> 19:25.822
- You are Touda, aren't you?
- I'm Guren.

19:26.165 --> 19:28.534
Seimei gave me this name...

19:28.534 --> 19:31.298
- And I like it.
- Grandfather...

19:32.371 --> 19:35.775
That's right! I remember
everything now!

19:35.775 --> 19:39.579
My grandfather sealed
my second sight.

19:39.579 --> 19:42.315
He said, "It's not good to
see too much.",

19:42.315 --> 19:44.117
and then sealed my power.

19:44.117 --> 19:47.987
When the time comes
and you really need to,

19:47.987 --> 19:49.750
you'll be able to see.

19:50.123 --> 19:53.217
Well, all your hard work
has paid off.

19:53.759 --> 19:55.862
- Mokkun!
- Don't call me Mokkun.

19:55.862 --> 19:58.854
- Seimei's grandson!
- Don't call me grandson!

19:59.398 --> 20:01.601
You're Mokkun when
you're in this form!

20:01.601 --> 20:04.627
No way!
Stop calling me Mokkun!

20:06.973 --> 20:08.634
A bird?

20:13.746 --> 20:17.182
- What is this?
- That's a magic letter.

20:20.620 --> 20:24.490
I see! So you can see now?

20:24.490 --> 20:27.994
But you have to be able to
handle things like that alone.

20:27.994 --> 20:30.062
Bye, Seimei.

20:30.062 --> 20:31.831
Bye, Seimei?

20:31.831 --> 20:36.131
That means he has been
watching us the whole time!?

20:40.806 --> 20:44.610
I can only think that
he enjoys giving me trouble!

20:44.610 --> 20:46.679
Come on. Don't say that.

20:46.679 --> 20:50.516
But this time I can face him
with my head held high.

20:50.516 --> 20:54.954
You exorcised that giant skull
without my help.

20:54.954 --> 20:56.114
Yeah.

21:00.359 --> 21:04.989
Well, you were very impressive
against that giant skull.

21:07.133 --> 21:09.835
But though you defeated it
on your own,

21:09.835 --> 21:13.202
the destruction of that
old house was unnecessary.

21:21.881 --> 21:27.080
That... cunning old man!!

21:42.969 --> 21:54.313
I heard your voice inside
the deep darkness

21:54.313 --> 22:05.791
Just your phrase "I believe"
echoed in my heart

22:05.791 --> 22:11.530
You always stayed by my side

22:11.530 --> 22:17.093
You always gave me courage

22:19.438 --> 22:29.749
In order to continue protecting
our future

22:29.749 --> 22:36.389
I promise you, my beloved

22:36.389 --> 22:41.727
I won't give up

22:41.727 --> 22:47.466
I will keep overcoming my limits

22:47.466 --> 22:54.338
Surely surely surely

23:00.079 --> 23:02.639
Next Episode

23:23.436 --> 23:25.705
Next on Shonen Onmyouji...

23:25.705 --> 23:26.772
Episode 2.

23:26.772 --> 23:27.173
Episode 2
The Palace Burns at Twilight
Episode 2.

